WEBVTT

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.460
Run!

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.040
What is it?

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.890
About yesterday...

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:25.470
Right.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:28.470
Run, you dropped your notebook!

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:38.480
What's up?

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.110
I-I-I-I-I'm sorry!

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:44.200
I'll forget all about it, so please don't kill me!

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.070
I'm sorry...

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:46.240
What are you talking about?

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.950
This notebook.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:51.620
It's that one used to curse people you have a grudge against, right?

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.250
No, it's not.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.750
This is my exchange notebook with Tooru.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.960
That's one of Tooru's pages.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.050
Then what are all these names for?

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.010
A memory test!

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:06.680
We're seeing who can write down the most names of people they've met.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.810
<i>Why, exactly?</i>

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.930
But man, her memory's good.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.980
I'll bet I couldn't beat her.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:17.400
Not to mention, all the names turn foreign-sounding halfway through.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.570
Did Tooru live abroad at one point?

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:20.690
Uh-uh.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:23.570
Starting there are characters from manga she's read.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:26.160
Oh, that explains the strange names.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.660
Justine?

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:32.160
Ooh. Michelle Richard.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.210
Jule Auguste Gianne.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:37.340
Marie-Françoise Victoire!

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:38.880
Oh?

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.460
Dovoch Hekenovich.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.840
François Poronac Haque.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.140
Michel Bomparnasse.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.680
O'Brien Vukovich.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.720
Alessandro Galexon.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.390
Paul Ginades!

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:55.270
Andreas Banderas!

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:57.310
Grakios Andretti!

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:58.940
What's this?

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:01.780
Yuuko.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:04.320
What is it?

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.280
So what did Tooru say?

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:12.410
She said she had something to show us, so come over.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:14.660
I wonder what it is?

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:18.790
But I've never been to Tooru's place before, so I'm pretty excited!

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.000
Neither have I.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.340
Wonder what kind of place it is?

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:24.260
You'll see soon.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:29.010
Right here!

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:34.270
That's quite the nice apartment she lives in.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.180
Let's go!

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.060
Right.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:40.770
Gosh, that Tooru. She didn't have to go home early just to clean up.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.690
Maybe there's something she doesn't want you to see?

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.200
What's wrong?

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.580
This feels like a foot massager! It's so nice!

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.460
Quit acting like an old lady and hurry up!

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.090
Tooru! We're here!

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:05.010
It's open! Come in!

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.010
Okay!

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.760
Pardon the intrusion!

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.520
Tooru! We're coming in!

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:24.650
So messy!

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.450
Is Tooru bad at cleaning up?

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:30.870
Uh-uh.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:33.910
She's usually obsessively neat.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.450
In other words, this must be...

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.200
A ransacked room.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:38.830
Its owner, missing.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.080
And the windows, locked from the inside.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.040
A locked-room murder!

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:44.840
Except the front entrance was open.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:45.960
Oh?

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.670
She wasn't just being a slob.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:51.640
Take a look. The trash in the trash bin just got scattered around.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.890
In other words, the trash went for a walk.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:57.100
It's not like they have legs.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.310
Oh no! A human is coming!

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.740
It all makes sense!

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.490
In any case, should we clean up?

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:11.360
Yeah.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:14.740
I doubt it's what you were thinking, Run-chan.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.620
Sorry it's so messy.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.540
This little guy was tearing up the room.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:20.920
Little guy?

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.420
So cute!

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.220
Where'd you get this cat?

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.180
I picked him up this morning.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:33.470
It seems he was abandoned.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:40.060
I get it! Cats have legs too, don't they?

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.770
I have no idea what you mean, Run.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.810
A cat could be personified, too!

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:45.400
What are you talking about?

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.820
And then, I bet it'd be Tooru!

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:48.820
Tha-

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.950
... I think I could live with that.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.150
Right?

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.910
What's that supposed to mean?

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:58.370
See you!

00:07:58.390 --> 00:07:59.950
See you tomorrow!

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.830
Say bye to the kitty for me!

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.460
See you later!

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:09.340
It's gotten colder. You okay, Tooru?

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.210
Yeah.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:11.420
That's right!

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.590
Want to grab something to eat on the way back?

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:16.050
Sure. I'd like something sweet.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.350
Then we could go to a family restaurant.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.220
Let's head through the shopping district.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:21.850
The shopping district, huh?

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:24.980
In that case, can we stop by somewhere on the way?

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:31.360
If I remember, it was somewhere around here...

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:32.990
Where are we headed?

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:34.570
I want to buy a collar.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:36.160
Ah, I see.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:39.290
While we're at it, some cat toys, and various other stuff.

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.700
Toys?

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.040
In that case, I know a place!

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:48.840
I'm sure they'll sell them here, no problem!

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:50.920
They'll sell them, no problem.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:53.010
But there's a huge problem!

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.720
Welcome!

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:04.190
<i>A white cat, so...</i>

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:05.600
<i>what color would look good?</i>

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.650
<i>Red? Blue?</i>

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:10.480
<i>Look at how serious she is.</i>

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:13.240
You must really care for that cat.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:16.610
I really care for you, too, Run-chan.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:19.530
I know~

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:20.950
That tickles...

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.830
Welcome to G-N's!

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.670
Thank you for your patience.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.380
Please, have a seat.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.710
Tooru, you can have the sofa seat.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:32.590
No, you have it, Run-chan.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.590
Then let's just sit together!

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.020
Ah, oh yeah.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.020
About my cat.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.060
I can never decide at the drink bar.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:54.780
How many flavors are you putting in?

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.700
Five-delicious-flavors-at-once mixed juice!

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:01.950
So you haven't decided on the cat's name yet.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:03.370
Yeah...

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:05.500
I can't come up with a good one.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.710
Why not name it after a sweet or a juice?

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.210
Since you like them.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:10.710
Ah, that's a good idea.

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.880
What I've got here right now are...

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:18.720
cola, cider, ramune, ginger ale, and melon soda, so...

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:21.260
putting them all together, you get...

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:22.830
"Carbonation"!

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.140
We're back!

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.940
How've you been doing?

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.820
Starting today, you'll be named "Carbonation"!

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.530
He's very well-behaved.

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:38.150
He runs wild now and then, though.

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.240
Carbonation, that collar looks good on you!

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.660
Such a cutie!

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:45.700
Hm?

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:46.910
Are you hungry?

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.790
We'll feed you right away.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:51.420
Oh, we got you some toys, too,

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.670
so let's play after you eat!

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:55.920
Run-chan.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:57.050
Let's talk about something.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:02.090
<i>I ended up not getting any attention from Run-chan.</i>

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.210
Good morning, Carbonation.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:48.850
It's that late already?

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:50.350
I'd better change.

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:05.370
Bad boy. You'll get fur on my uniform.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.580
I don't have time to play with you.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:11.330
Temperatures will be very low this morning, continuing throughout the day.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:14.210
The chance of snow this afternoon is high,

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:17.210
so please be prepared as you leave home today.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.550
Oh, all right.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.520
I'll be off, then.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:05.800
Morning, Tooru!

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:10.350
It's gotten even colder today.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:15.560
Apparently it's going to snow today, Run-chan.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:16.690
Well, according to the forecast.

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:17.150
Really?

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.900
Wait just a sec!

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:30.450
What was it?

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:34.830
Ta-dah!

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.120
I brought syrup!

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:39.920
For the snow?

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:40.460
Yep.

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.180
Yuuko-chan, morning!

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:49.140
Good morning!

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.100
Another cold morning today.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:51.680
Yeah.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:53.350
Morning.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:55.560
Morn-

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:59.690
Nagi! What's with that outfit?

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:02.480
The forecast said snow, so I made suitable preparations.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:05.320
You look like an assassin! How cool!

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:07.320
Don't you mean a pervert?

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:10.700
Honestly.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:14.870
Why do we have to come to school in this blasted cold?

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:17.710
It's only natural. We're students.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:25.300
Don't you think they should make it winter break from the end of fall to the start of spring?

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.720
You must hate winter.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.890
Despite constantly ranting about how hot summer was.

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:34.220
When the snow comes falling, I just lose the will to live.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:35.850
What's with the depressing talk?

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:38.690
Snowy days are full of fun things!

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:41.940
Like making snowmen, or making igloos,

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:43.770
or having snowball fights!

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:47.400
Nagi-chan, you should pray for snow, too!

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:49.490
Huh?

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:55.950
Did you even listen to a single thing I said?

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:56.500
Huh?

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.090
It's not going to snow.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:11.390
I'm sure of it.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:21.230
Haven't given up yet, I see.

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:23.860
Well, I've half given up.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.230
Just completely give up.

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:29.240
Whoa! It's started snowing!

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:29.610
Huh?

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:31.410
What?

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:34.410
Awesome!

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:35.280
Cool!

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:39.120
It's true. It's snowing!

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:40.330
Ugh.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.040
The weather changes on a dime.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:44.170
Run, isn't that wonderf-

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:44.460
Huh?

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:45.710
She's gone!

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:47.750
It's here!

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:49.050
Lunch! Lunch!

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.610
Looks like it'll pile up.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:10.940
It's coming down hard!

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:12.860
If a lot piles up,

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:15.120
I've always wanted to try this once!

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:20.120
Get buried so deep, you can't see the bottom!

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:23.290
Just like in a manga.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:25.380
If I jumped from here, I bet I could do it!

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:26.130
What?

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:27.710
That's a little...

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:29.840
Ah, then what about from the roof?

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:32.930
I don't think it'll work.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:55.320
It piled up!

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:56.450
Amazing!

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:58.330
All right! Let's go!

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:03.710
Yay!

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:09.920
Run-chan.

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:11.130
Did she die?

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:18.640
She's eating it!

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:19.890
Run-chan, don't do that!

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:22.600
Hey, let's all jump in!

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:31.530
Gosh, don't do that so suddenly!

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:34.650
What was that, out of nowhere?

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.280
That's dangerous, you know.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.450
Huh? What?

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:41.120
Yuuko-chan, that's a funny pose!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:43.330
Nice one, Yuuko.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:45.210
Gosh!

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:46.710
Snow...

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:47.460
Huh?

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:50.880
Snow is...

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.210
quite warm.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.590
Nagi?

00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:59.390
Nagi, are you okay?

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:01.430
You look cold.

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:02.470
That's right!

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:02.930
Huh?

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.930
Nagi-chan, we'll warm you up!

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:10.560
What are you doing, Run-chan?

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:13.690
I'm making an igloo for Nagi-chan.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:14.780
Ah!

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.820
I hear those are warm!

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:18.240
I'll help!

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:41.550
There we go.

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:43.720
Nagi-chan, it's done!

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:46.730
Looks cramped.

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.810
Nagi, feeling warmer?

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.770
Yeah, better than outside.

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:52.150
Thank goodness.

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:58.780
You're wide open, Yuuko-chan! Hi-yah!

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.500
Here I come, too!

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:10.420
Now you've done it!

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:04.950
After playing around so much outside,

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.320
I'm surprised I didn't catch a cold.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.910
"I caught a cold. -Yuuko"

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.500
Why did you catch one?

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:18.670
Oh.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:23.720
"I've got a fever of 38 degrees. -Tooru"

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:30.100
"Looks like I've caught a cold. -Run"

00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:29.420
Come here.

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:37.970
Nice and warm.

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:42.310
S...

00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:43.940
So cold...

00:23:47.530 --> 00:23:48.740
Okay, everyone!

00:23:48.740 --> 00:23:50.240
Let's shovel with all we've got!

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:52.070
Yes ma'am...

00:23:57.670 --> 00:24:00.430
It's almost time to bid farewell to everyone, isn't it?

00:24:00.430 --> 00:24:01.810
Eh? Already?!

00:24:01.810 --> 00:24:03.110
Isn't it too soon?

00:24:03.110 --> 00:24:04.630
Wait, it's already winter?!

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:05.830
It came fast, huh?

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:08.040
What did we do last winter, anyway?

00:24:08.040 --> 00:24:10.300
Well, we were getting ready for the high school entrance exam...

00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:12.840
That's right, we spent a lot ot time studying, didn't we?

00:24:12.840 --> 00:24:15.800
Although Yutaka was always the one teaching Mipo-rin!

00:24:16.280 --> 00:24:17.310
Don't lie!

00:24:17.620 --> 00:24:19.850
Next time, on A Channel, Birthday.

00:24:19.850 --> 00:24:22.190
Everyone, do your best at studying for your exams!

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:24.450
What month do you think it is?
